Z||000000||acehilton||06-27-2001||10:24 PM||||Howdy all,<P>My 86 coupe has a little overheating problem.  At the drive thru at Wendy's, I keep overheating (the smell of hot coolant ruins the tast of a spicy chicken sandwich).<BR>I finally figured out the fan is not kicking on.  Either I have to start going inside to order lunch, or I have to fix my cooling system.<P>I checked out the relays and switches as per other posts on the forum, and have narrowed it down to the fan motor.  Now for the question.<P>A quick search on car parts.com revealed about a dozen different fan motors.  AC Delco lists 2 different part #'s for the fan I need (HD w/AC), 15-8498 is listed as a fan motor kit for $67.88.  Part #15-8221 is listed for $190.63.  I am willing to bet one of them is just the motor, and one is the entire assembly (fan and all).  There are also a few after market motors listed.<P>Does anyone have any recommendations on what they have used (i.e. which motor to buy) to solve the same problem?<BR>  <BR>It definitely is the motor, I used a power supply to put voltage directly to the motor, nothing happened.<P>Thanks in advance for everyones help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||06-27-2001||11:32 PM||||AC delco, just the mtr.||||reg||1
